# What must never enter a build context.
#
# The first three are the same rules scripts/verify-repo-hygiene.sh enforces for
# Git, for the same reasons and with a sharper edge: a build context is copied
# in full before any Dockerfile line runs, so a missing entry here does not just
# slow the build, it puts 5.6 GB of model weights and a reader's documents
# inside an image that may later be pushed somewhere.

# Model weights. Mounted at run time, never built in. See infra/README.md.
models/

# Uploaded documents and anything generated from them.
data/generated/
data/uploads/

# Secrets. Passed as environment at run time; never baked into a layer, where
# they would survive in the image history even if a later layer deleted them.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git/
.github/
.venv/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/node_modules/
apps/web/.next/
apps/web/out/
.vscode/
scratchpad/
*.pdf
*.wav
*.pth
*.bin
